<title>BRAZIL: Brazil January daily average exports at $157.8 mln.</title>
<headline>Brazil January daily average exports at $157.8 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian exports so far in January averaged only $157.8 million a day, the Ministry of Industry and Commerce said.</p>
<p>The Ministry said in a statement that up to end of the third week of the month exports totalled $1.894 billion.</p>
<p>The Ministry said that average daily exports in the third week of January were $153.2 million against $162.4 million in the second week and $158 million on the first two working days of the month.</p>
<p>Exports in January 1996 totalled $3.473 billion with a daily average of $157.9 million.</p>
<p>((-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 5561 322 6962))</p>
